arm64: dts: h713: give the AFBD scanout to a KMS driver

Adds display@5600000 for the AFBD KMS driver, and answers a question the
video-decode work left open: what DECD is for. DECD probes and works, but
nothing uses it -- its registers are not in the scanout fetch path -- while
it holds exactly the two resources a display driver needs: the AFBD
register window at 0x05600000 and the 60 Hz vsync interrupt on SPI 110.
Two drivers cannot own those, so dec@5600000 is disabled here and the
window goes to the driver that puts pixels on the panel. DECD is still
built (CONFIG_SUNXI_DECD=m) and the node is one word from coming back if a
job is ever found for it.

The new node takes only the AFBD range. It does NOT take the 0x05700000
TVTOP range DECD also mapped, and it does not carry `resets`: the panel is
brought up before Linux by U-Boot's h713_disp and the MIPS co-processor,
and asserting rst_bus_disp would kill a display this driver cannot bring
back. Leaving the reset out of the DT makes that a property of the
hardware description rather than a rule the C code has to remember.

uboot-scanout@6c100000 becomes a shared-dma-pool so framebuffers can be
allocated from it. It stays no-map: on arm64 rmem_dma_setup() has no
objection (the no-map requirement is #ifdef CONFIG_ARM), and
dma_init_coherent_memory() memremaps it write-combine, which is what a
framebuffer wants. The alternative -- allocating from the 16 MiB system
CMA pool -- would have taken two 3.5 MiB framebuffers out from under
cedrus, which decodes into that same pool.

It also grows from 8 to 16 MiB. At 1280x720x4 the old size held exactly
the two scanout slots U-Boot uses and nothing else, which is enough to
flip between but not to also serve a client's buffers or the fbdev
console. The region is above every other reservation, so growing it takes
memory from the kernel's general pool and from nothing else.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -103,9 +103,22 @@
 		 * the back at 0x6c500000. Double buffering flips the AFBD
 		 * source address (0x05600178) between them, so both are live
 		 * scanout targets and the kernel must not use either.
+		 *
+		 * shared-dma-pool, so the KMS driver allocates framebuffers
+		 * here rather than from the 16 MiB system CMA pool, which
+		 * cedrus decodes into. no-map is correct on arm64:
+		 * rmem_dma_setup() only demands a mapping under CONFIG_ARM, and
+		 * dma_init_coherent_memory() memremaps the region
+		 * write-combine, which is what a framebuffer wants.
+		 *
+		 * 16 MiB, not 8: U-Boot's two slots fill 8 MiB exactly, leaving
+		 * nothing for a client's buffers or the fbdev console. This
+		 * region sits above every other reservation, so growing it
+		 * takes memory from the kernel's general pool and nothing else.
 		 */
 		framebuf_reserved: uboot-scanout@6c100000 {
-			reg = <0x6c100000 0x800000>;
+			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
+			reg = <0x6c100000 0x1000000>;
 			no-map;
 		};
 	};
@@ -1597,6 +1610,33 @@
 			 * a divider beneath a live panel. Match what is there.
 			 */
 			clock-frequency = <100000000>;
+			/*
+			 * Disabled: display@5600000 owns this register window
+			 * and SPI 110 now. DECD probes and works but has no
+			 * job -- its registers are not in the scanout fetch
+			 * path -- and two drivers cannot hold one window and
+			 * one interrupt. Still built as a module; this is one
+			 * word from coming back if a use is ever found.
+			 */
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
+		/*
+		 * AFBD scanout, driven as KMS. Adopts the display U-Boot's
+		 * h713_disp brought up and drives buffer selection and page
+		 * flips only -- never timing, the LVDS PHY, or the display
+		 * reset. The missing `resets` property is deliberate: asserting
+		 * rst_bus_disp would kill a panel this driver cannot bring
+		 * back, so the hardware description withholds the means.
+		 */
+		display: display@5600000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h713-afbd";
+			reg = <0x05600000 0x400>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 110 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_AFBD>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_BUS_DISP>;
+			clock-names = "clk_afbd", "clk_bus_disp";
+			memory-region = <&framebuf_reserved>;
 			status = "okay";
 		};
 
